  "text": {
    "intro": "Mrs Pell's secondhand bookshop shelves by a system she alone understands, and she has gone to Margate for a fortnight.\nFive volumes are involved. Determine each volume's shelf and price.\n- **Volume**: a guide to fungi, a treatise on clocks, a book of sea shanties, a water-stained atlas and a Latin primer.\n- **Shelf** (listed from lower to higher): the bottom shelf, the second shelf, the third shelf, the fourth shelf and the fifth shelf.\n- **Pencilled price**: half a crown; seven and six; four shillings; ninepence; and a guinea.\nEvery volume has a different shelf and price, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "A guide to fungi and the fifth shelf are exactly one shelf apart in shelf order, in one direction or the other. A water-stained atlas sits on the fifth shelf.",
      "The volume that is priced at four shillings sits on the second shelf.",
      "A Latin primer is lower than the second shelf in shelf order.",
      "A guide to fungi is exactly one shelf lower than the volume that is priced at seven and six, with no shelf in between.",
      "The volume that is priced at a guinea is exactly one shelf lower than a book of sea shanties, with no shelf in between.",
